\ Reference output for predictmeans from Genstat REML (written for Genstat 21+;
\ the first run may need small syntax fixes - please send the output window
\ or the .out file, not values typed by hand).
\ Questions: (1) which Kenward-Roger df Genstat gives when a whole plot is
\ missing (pbkrtest 9.25, SAS 8.35 for the Variety differences);
\ (2) its F tests and df for an AR(1) repeated-measures model with missing
\ values (SAS: dev/sas/pm-reference-ar1.sas, same data).

\ ---- 1. Oats split plot, the whole plot (Block I, GoldenRain) missing ----
\ Variety 1 GoldenRain, 2 Marvellous, 3 Victory (alphabetical, as SAS)
UNITS [NVALUES=72]
FACTOR [LEVELS=6] Block
FACTOR [LABELS=!t(GoldenRain, Marvellous, Victory)] Variety
FACTOR [LEVELS=!(0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6)] Nitro
VARIATE Yield
READ Block, Variety, Nitro, Yield
1 1 0.0 *   1 1 0.2 *   1 1 0.4 *   1 1 0.6 *
1 2 0.0 105   1 2 0.2 140   1 2 0.4 118   1 2 0.6 156
1 3 0.0 111   1 3 0.2 130   1 3 0.4 157   1 3 0.6 174
2 1 0.0 70   2 1 0.2 108   2 1 0.4 126   2 1 0.6 149
2 2 0.0 96   2 2 0.2 124   2 2 0.4 121   2 2 0.6 144
2 3 0.0 61   2 3 0.2 91   2 3 0.4 97   2 3 0.6 100
3 1 0.0 60   3 1 0.2 102   3 1 0.4 89   3 1 0.6 96
3 2 0.0 89   3 2 0.2 129   3 2 0.4 132   3 2 0.6 124
3 3 0.0 68   3 3 0.2 64   3 3 0.4 112   3 3 0.6 86
4 1 0.0 64   4 1 0.2 103   4 1 0.4 132   4 1 0.6 133
4 2 0.0 70   4 2 0.2 89   4 2 0.4 104   4 2 0.6 117
4 3 0.0 74   4 3 0.2 89   4 3 0.4 81   4 3 0.6 122
5 1 0.0 80   5 1 0.2 82   5 1 0.4 94   5 1 0.6 126
5 2 0.0 63   5 2 0.2 70   5 2 0.4 109   5 2 0.6 99
5 3 0.0 62   5 3 0.2 90   5 3 0.4 100   5 3 0.6 116
6 1 0.0 89   6 1 0.2 82   6 1 0.4 86   6 1 0.6 104
6 2 0.0 97   6 2 0.2 99   6 2 0.4 119   6 2 0.6 121
6 3 0.0 53   6 3 0.2 74   6 3 0.4 118   6 3 0.6 113
:
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=Variety*Nitro] RANDOM=Block/Variety
REML [PRINT=model, components, waldtests, means; PTERMS=Variety + Nitro + Variety.Nitro; \
      PSE=differences; METHOD=AI] Yield

\ ---- 2. AR(1) repeated measures, 5 of 48 values missing ----
\ Group 1 = A, 2 = B
UNITS [NVALUES=48]
FACTOR [LEVELS=12] Subj
FACTOR [LEVELS=2] Group
FACTOR [LEVELS=4] Time
VARIATE Y
READ Subj, Group, Time, Y
1 1 1 *   1 1 2 10.29   1 1 3 10.02   1 1 4 10.27
2 1 1 10.34   2 1 2  9.86   2 1 3 11.68   2 1 4 11.96
3 1 1 10.07   3 1 2 *   3 1 3 12.44   3 1 4 11.62
4 1 1 11.58   4 1 2 12.61   4 1 3 *   4 1 4 11.74
5 1 1 11.58   5 1 2 11.99   5 1 3 12.17   5 1 4 12.34
6 1 1 10.22   6 1 2  9.39   6 1 3  9.60   6 1 4 *
7 2 1 12.37   7 2 2 12.68   7 2 3 12.56   7 2 4 12.95
8 2 1 12.10   8 2 2 12.39   8 2 3 13.15   8 2 4 12.98
9 2 1 10.85   9 2 2 10.36   9 2 3 11.22   9 2 4 14.00
10 2 1 13.06   10 2 2 13.09   10 2 3 14.72   10 2 4 13.51
11 2 1 10.32   11 2 2  9.20   11 2 3 11.97   11 2 4 *
12 2 1 10.35   12 2 2 11.33   12 2 3 11.86   12 2 4 12.66
:
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=Group*Time] RANDOM=Subj.Time
VSTRUCTURE [TERMS=Subj.Time] FACTOR=Time; MODEL=AR; ORDER=1
\ MVINCLUDE=yvariate keeps the units with a missing Y, so Subj.Time is the residual
\ term (with the AR(1) structure) instead of a random term next to a new residual
REML [PRINT=model, components, waldtests, means; PTERMS=Group + Time + Group.Time; \
      PSE=differences; METHOD=AI; MVINCLUDE=yvariate] Y
STOP
